  "description": "Powered, steerable airships (dirigibles) using helium or hydrogen for lift within a rigid, semi-rigid, or non-rigid (blimp) envelope. Internal combustion or electric motors drive propellers for thrust; rudders and elevators provide directional control. Gas airships achieve far greater payload and endurance than hot-air balloons, enabling long-range surveillance, cargo transport, and advertising. Lift depends on gas density rather than sustained heating.",
